    "summary": "The complete candidate combines PR240 sender and PR238 saved Audit settings. Current Admins read and save tenant-bound settings through web with origin/CSRF checks and encrypted credentials. Audit logs owns event projection, settings, and the isolated one-shot sender; System logs remains internal and separate. App supplies the settings service and owns its SQL lifetime. The sender has no production caller yet. This dependency merge adds no new Test operation, capture, queue, paid resource, schema, or deployment. Full-main review retains the inherited container, external, contract, deployment, policy and dependency impact. S2-02b implementation and final review are pending. System diagnostics now use concrete SystemLogger with a required synchronous SystemLogSink; console and OTel adapters own output, and every constructor is migrated. Preparation and System/Audit separation stay unchanged. This preserves the System sink CR inherited from PR240.",
